<title>USA: Allergan's Alphagan wins okay in Britain.</title>
<headline>Allergan's Alphagan wins okay in Britain.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allergan Inc on Tuesday said it has received approval from the Medicines Control Agency to market Alphagan in the United Kingdom for treating open-angle glaucoma and ocular hypertension.</p>
<p>In a statement, Allergan said it will seek approval to sell Alphagan, or brimonidine, in the balance of the European community through the mutual recognition filings.</p>
<p>Alphagan is a selective alpha2 agonist that lowers intraocular pressure with minimal effects on cardiovascular and pulmonary parameters. Glaucoma, an eye disease associated with intraocular pressure, can cause blindness.</p>
</text>
